{
  "locale": "en",
  "_doc": [
    "AUTHORED GRAMMAR TABLE for the Asking Bench (tool #36). Every surface",
    "string a child can ever see is IN THIS FILE, verbatim. The tool never",
    "concatenates a morpheme and never inflects anything — gate M-CLOSURE",
    "proves it. So a mistake here is a mistake on a classroom board, and",
    "the only defences are this file being small enough to proofread and",
    "the native panel that authored it.",
    "",
    "RESTRICTIONS, each one gated, each disarming a class of wrongness:",
    "  * NOMINATIVE ONLY. The noun is always the subject and never moves.",
    "  * 3rd-person NOUN subjects only (no pronouns) — disarms *am I*.",
    "  * no separable verbs, no negation.",
    "",
    "ENGLISH IS THE INTERESTING ONE and it is why the tool works: the",
    "transformation depends on WHICH VERB the child picked. `is` fronts",
    "with nothing arriving; a lexical present needs a *do* that was never",
    "there AND reshapes the verb; a past needs *did* AND sends the verb",
    "back to its base; a modal just fronts. Four structurally different",
    "answers from one lever."
  ],
