  "_notes": "en authored by the builder as the pilot table; the other ten come from their own native panels and are NOT translations of this. Deliberately excluded: pronoun subjects (would need *am I*), separable/phrasal verbs (*The dog runs away* splits in de and is a different lesson), negation, and the whole wh-question family (owned outright by wren-question-window L.K.1.d). A MODAL LIVES IN ITS OWN FRAME because it needs a main verb after it — the first draft let S-V admit a modal and rendered \"The dog can.\", which is not a sentence. No gate can know that; the frame has to make it unreachable, and M-WELLFORMED now asserts the pairing. `be` is present only in the S-be-ADJ frame because *The dog is the ball* is nonsense — the frame's verbClass list is what keeps that unreachable.",
